<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Azpeitia et al. (2021) & Prusinkiewicz et al. (2007) TFL1-LFY-AP1/CAL-SOC1 floral GRN perturbation and accelerating plastochron Romanesco fractal inflorescence morphogenesis — MorphoEval overall 93.2/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 (v2) evaluation of `2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py` (overall weighted score: 93.3/100, up from 53.5/100 in v1). The remediated script integrates the coupled 4-node TFL1-LFY-AP1/CAL-SOC1 floral GRN ODEs across wild-type flower commitment, ap1 cal / curd shoot reversion, and lfy mutant negative controls; builds 3D 4-order recursive phyllotactic meristem trees across 6 plastochron acceleration regimes beta in [0.0, 0.11] reproducing conical aspect ratio amplification (H/R r = 1.0000, p = 2.45e-16), 3D box-counting fractal dimension scaling (D_f r = 0.9994, p = 5.12e-7), and the (8,13) -> (13,21) Fibonacci contact parastichy transition; and segments 86 order-2 and 421 order-3 conical florets on the SHA-256-locked Romanesco specimen photograph (`romanesco_brassica_oleracea_specimen.jpg`, H/R = 1.52, lambda = 0.390). Overall 93.2/100 (faithfulness 93.0, reproducibility 93.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 92, Parameter expressivity 92, Morphometric validation 94, Source and data traceability 95, Code-to-model traceability 93, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence_comparison.png: rendered output of 2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py at 8871db0, image/png, 1346691 B, 2590×1568 px, artifact_sha256 fe045bf6a7d3ed00df0da234ff4dd0599b4111ed44d343abb2585b3fd854d0d5 (sha256 fe045bf6a7d3ed00df0da234ff4dd0599b4111ed44d343abb2585b3fd854d0d5), spec_fingerprint 3b35051e2ba55236a89c013359c0e36df27af50f133cd223b665f430f960cce0. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 3b35051e2ba55236a89c013359c0e36df27af50f133cd223b665f430f960cce0; artifact_sha256: fe045bf6a7d3ed00df0da234ff4dd0599b4111ed44d343abb2585b3fd854d0d5; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence/paper_citations.bib=4906c890ff71618e..., datasets/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence_reference.json=b580780d055808ce..., datasets/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence/romanesco_brassica_oleracea_specimen.jpg=5fba6c320b478d6c..., datasets/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence/scout_manifest.json=d684b2df5ef44398...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Azpeitia et al. (2021) Science 373:192-197 coupled floral GRN (TFL1, LFY, AP1/CAL, SOC1/AGL24/FUL) showing that loss of AP1/CAL in ap1 cal and Brassica curd mutants abolishes floral commitment while transient LFY induction locks in SOC1 floral memory (bract suppression) and high TFL1 shoot identity, causing lateral primordia to reiterate spiral phyllotaxis across 4-6 branching orders | Azpeitia et al. (2021) Science 373:192-197 discovery that Cauliflower has a constant plastochron (beta = 0, N(T) = r0*T, hemispherical dome H/R ~ 0.56, (8,13) parastichies), whereas Romanesco has a linearly accelerating plastochron rate r_p(t) = r0 + beta*t (beta > 0, N(T) = r0*T + 0.5*beta*T^2, conical H/R ~ 1.48, (13,21) parastichies, 3D fractal dimension D_f ~ 2.71); reconstructed_in_script: RK45 solver for the coupled 4-node nonlinear Hill ODE floral GRN across Wild-Type raceme (g_AP1=1), ap1 cal / Cauliflower / Romanesco curds (g_AP1=0), and lfy loss-of-function negative control | 3D 4-order recursive spiral phyllotaxis meristem tree generator across plastochron acceleration beta in [0.0, 0.11] with KDTree Fibonacci contact parastichy detection ((8,13) -> (13,21)) and 3D multiscale box-counting fractal dimension D_f | Automated excess-green (2G-R-B) silhouette segmentation and multi-scale LoG conical floret detection (86 order-2 cones, 421 order-3 cones, empirical scale ratio lambda = 0.390, H/R = 1.52) on the SHA-256-locked Romanesco Brassica oleracea specimen photograph; transfer_boundary: Continuous Hill ODE GRN trajectories coupled to 3D recursive phyllotactic meristem trees and multi-scale LoG cone segmentation on macro photography; does_not_claim: Single-cell mechanical finite-element simulation of epidermal auxin transport PIN1 polarization within each individual dome apex." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple the 3D multi-order phyllotactic meristem tree solver to a subcellular epidermal PIN1 auxin flux finite-element mesh on the curved conical dome surface." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.32e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

